{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/3986","id":4917785502,"node_id":"PR_kwDOU-508s8AAAABJR9zng","html_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3986","diff_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3986.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3986.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/3986","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/3986/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/3986/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/issues/3986/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/statuses/a693da700af272252d701b36614922fd838efdd2","number":3986,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Audit current R437 whole-word translation under retained physical contracts","user":{"login":"Clear1nsight","id":22630354,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjMwMzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22630354?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight","html_url":"https://github.com/Clear1nsight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## Current-source contribution\r\n\r\nExtends Nick Petalas's #2989 compiler-correspondence audit to the complete current R437/OQ4 event skeleton at #3647 head a24f9ff95c12fd0b6792e3f710569237efd72db2. New package: `research/r437-whole-word-refinement`; no shared-code or selected-frontier changes.\r\n\r\n- Actual retained Driver versus actual compiler/dispatcher: 288 calls, 903,456 residual sites, 7,035,840 ordered local/family XOR input-output triples, 29 global checkpoints and 12,336,607 emitted symbolic macros, at one formal low label. All arbitrary initial family contents remain symbolic. Each disposal and final staged/private cleanup is checked.\r\n- Five semantic mutants reject, including destructive clone, lost private output, stale scatter, omitted private disposal and reversed XOR roles. Tiny two-low tests cover both mode0 and mode1.\r\n- The unchanged `Machine.run` loop is exercised under explicit recursive-cut contract actions at depths 0,1,2,17. This adds loop-composition coverage; it does not execute physical CALL/RETURN.\r\n- The conditional ordering theorem and omitted-owner admission guard are **credited restatements of #2989**, not new discoveries. The useful delta is current R437/OQ4 whole-source coverage beyond its eight reduced GL2(F3) words.\r\n\r\n## Qualification\r\n\r\nThis is a differential source-reuse check and a conditional theorem adaptation, not an independent numerical implementation. The compiler's append-only list is streamed in the checker to bound memory; branches and emitted operations are unchanged. Packet operations and residuals are opaque expression constructors. One formal low does not enumerate GL64; abstract good-block residual symbols do not test real good/fallback bodies. Primitive algebra, high fields, full production volume, source/stock/history, physical parking, time/visited-space, precision and ordinary/native/router premises remain open. No supplier admission or new kappa.\r\n\r\nThe paired operational-semantics/separation-relation and algebraic-expression approach isolates exactly this composition layer. The sibling transport/resource lanes remain separate contributions, not automatically admitted dependencies.\r\n\r\n## Validation and pins\r\n\r\nCanonical main and priority revision6: 20ecf2891d80b5acf18d980b2164fb44ea7faa90. Both retained R437 files match their exact upstream a24f9ff Git blobs, also retained through #3936. PR[3967](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3967) CI was checked PASS before this round. Full local symbolic generation: CPython3.12.3,234.03 seconds,208340 KiB peak RSS.\r\n\r\nRegistered replay, optimized semantic controls and actual Git-free quick export pass. The export run is deliberately the bounded quick scope. Changed compiler/template, missing word and symlinked dispatcher controls reject. Reproduce:\r\n\r\n`python3 -B scripts/research_package.py --package research/r437-whole-word-refinement`\r\n\r\nSOURCES/TASK/VERIFY retain exact provenance, scope and commands. No historical full replay, Lean or Docker was run. Hosted CI is reported separately from local success.\r\n\r\n## Coordination and credit\r\n\r\nExplicit user assignment refines `independent-moment`; team claim: https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3967#issuecomment-6262146714. Live overlap found #3967/#3950/#3936/#3724/#3690; the team then found and read canonical #2989, and narrowed the novelty claim accordingly. Search coverage is partial, not a novelty certificate.\r\n\r\nNick Petalas/#2989; Jose Manuel/#2809/#2195 and numerical/ordinary lineage; David Arias/#2753; ywz65 parking/staging; ai-nanachi R437/OQ4; zxv/#3690; Ali Romman/#1043 and retained helper/native/compiler/owner/outer contributors. Chris R/Clear1nsight's #3936/#3950/#3967 source/stream/return audits are predecessor context. New source audit, adaptation and packaging by Chris R with substantial OpenAI Codex assistance. Full notices and attribution are in the package.\r\n\r\nOpen next questions: independently admit actual current chart separation; prove complete residual and recursive-cut contracts; attach the complete physical cost and visited-cell invoice without omitting the rest of the rank26 child or double-counting its internal rank7 COPY.\r\n\r\nPublication head `a693da700af272252d701b36614922fd838efdd2` passes exact 26-file package/input byte and canonical source-history verification plus whitespace checks. All three registered commands passed. Retained notice and input bytes preserve their original line endings. The separate current chart certificate is now public in PR #[3980](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/3980); it remains subject to its stated scope and review.\r\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-19T08:02:19Z","updated_at":"2026-10-19T08:03:22Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"0fd85da81e16bbe182e9256bab1ef3e8d5cef5cb","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Clear1nsight:audit/r437-whole-word-refinement-20261019","ref":"audit/r437-whole-word-refinement-20261019","repo":{"id":1423767139,"node_id":"R_kgDOVNz2Yw","name":"integer-mult-bounds","full_name":"Clear1nsight/integer-mult-bounds","owner":{"login":"Clear1nsight","id":22630354,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIyNjMwMzU0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/22630354?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight","html_url":"https://github.com/Clear1nsight","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Clear1nsight/subscrip